{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Ibn Majah","section":{"5":{"eng-name":"Establishing the Prayer and the Sunnah Regarding Them","ara-name":"كتاب إقامة الصلاة والسنة فيها"}},"section_detail":{"5":{"hadithnumber_first":803,"hadithnumber_last":1432,"arabicnumber_first":803,"arabicnumber_last":1432}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":929,"arabicnumber":929,"text":"Rapporté par Qabisah bin Hulb, dont le père a dit : Le Prophète (ﷺ) nous a dirigés dans la prière, et il avait l’habitude de partir d’un côté ou de l’autre (c’est-à-dire à droite ou à gauche)","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih Lighairihi"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}],"reference":{"book":5,"hadith":127},"chapter":{"id":33,"ara-name":"باب الاِنْصِرَافِ مِنَ الصَّلاَةِ ","eng-name":"Departing after completing the Prayer","isFirstHadith":true}}]}